  <data name="ReadmeTitle.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Readme</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ReadmeIntro.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>MSFS-UI-GENERATOR installs and sets up msfs-ui, a mod of the Microsoft Flight Simulator 2024 main menu: faster menus, a weather and time bar on Free Flight, favourite aircraft and liveries, an aircraft gallery and list, a setup panel and a tail number per livery.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ReadmeNoSimFile.Title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>No file of the simulator is modified</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ReadmeNoSimFile.Message" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The mod lives in its own package, msfs-ui, in the sim's Community folder. The sim's own files are only read: never changed, moved or deleted. Removing the package (Remove on the Home page, then a restart of the sim) brings the original menu back.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ReadmeHowHeader.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>How it works</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ReadmeHow1.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>1. The sim builds its main menu from components, and a package in the Community folder can stand in for one of them. When you generate the package, the app makes a copy of the menu's root component from your own sim, adds a small loader to it, and places the copy in the msfs-ui package. The sim then uses this copy instead of its own file, which stays untouched.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ReadmeHow2.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>2. When the menu opens, the loader starts the mod. The mod adds its panels and changes the menu in memory only: everything it does is undone when it unloads or when the sim closes. When it changes a setting of the sim (aircraft, livery, weather, time, traffic), it uses the same commands as the sim's own buttons.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ReadmeHow3.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>3. Your choices on the Features page are written in the package as a settings file, which the mod reads when it starts. Apply updates this file and reloads the mod while the sim runs: no restart is needed.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ReadmeHow4.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>4. What the mod remembers (favourites, tail numbers per livery, last weather and time choice, the gallery's view) is kept by the sim in its own storage, as it keeps its own preferences.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ReadmePagesHeader.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The pages</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ReadmePageHome.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Home</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ReadmePageHomeText.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Finds the sim, shows the state of the package, and installs (Generate &amp; install), reloads or removes it.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ReadmePageFeatures.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Features</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ReadmePageFeaturesText.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Turns each feature of the mod on or off and sets its options; Apply makes the change live.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ReadmePageCompatibility.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Compatibility</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ReadmePageCompatibilityText.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Checks that the sim still offers everything the mod uses, in its files and, while it runs, in its menu. Useful after a sim update.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ReadmePageLog.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Log</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ReadmePageLogText.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>What the app did, and the mod's own messages read from the running sim.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ReadmeUpdateHeader.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>After a sim update</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ReadmeUpdateText.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Use Generate &amp; install again, then restart the sim: the package has to copy the new version of the menu's root component. The Home page says when this is needed.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ReadmeFilesHeader.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Files of the app</value>
  </data>
  <data name="ReadmeFilesText.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>The package: &lt;Community folder&gt;\msfs-ui. The app's settings, chosen folders, theme and logs: %LOCALAPPDATA%\MSFS-UI-GENERATOR. Nothing else is written on the computer.</value>
  </data>
